FILE MANAGEMENT COMMANDS :
========================================

1.list all files and directories

a.long list shows detailed information directories , owner, size

command 1 : ll 

b.short list shows only files 

command 2 : ls (one line)

c.This command same as ll

command 3 : ls -l 

d.Shows the hidden file

command : ls -la or ll -a

here : 

l = long list
a = all files including hidden files

e. Shows hidden file in short list

command : ls -a

f.Show all files in human readable formate

command : ls -lh

g.Sort modification time newest first

command : ls -lt

h. Shows the modification files oldest to newest

command : ls -ltr

i. Shows inode number

command : ls -i

j.Shows long list with inode number

command : ls -li

k.shows directory itself instead of listing it contents

command : ls -ld 

example : ls -ld /opt

l.List files and subdirectories

 command : ls -R

 It will enter directories and show their contents too.

m.Sort files size Decending order [largest first]

 command : ls -S

n.Sort file size Acending order[smallest first]

 command : ls -Sr

o.Sort files by extension

 command : ls -X or ls -lX

p. Add symbols by files and directories

 command : ls -F

 / -> directories

 * -> files

 @ -> link

2.Shows Present Working Directory 

 command : pwd

3.Change Directory

 commad : cd 

 example : cd /opt

4.Move to back directory 

 command : cd ..

5. Move to home directory

  command : cd ~

6.Move to previous direcotory

 command : cd -

7.Stay in current direcotory

 command : cd .

Create Files and Directories
============================
8. Create empty file

 command : touch

 example : touch docker

 example : Create multiple files

 touch file1 file2 file3

9.Create a Directory

 command : mkdir

 example : mkdir project

 example : create multiple directories

 mkdir dir1 dir2 dir3

10.Create parent and child directories together

 command : mkdir -p

 example : mkdir -p devops/docker/project

 